   "summary": "The law rewrote section 114(f) and changed section 114(g) to set new statutory royalty procedures, new distribution rules, a mechanism for letters of direction, and a rule that preempts State escheatment or abandoned property laws for covered receipts [2018-115-264-114-1] [2018-115-264-114-3] [2018-115-264-114-5] [2018-115-264-114-6] [2018-115-264-114-13]. It overhauled section 115 by changing the compulsory license rules, adding a blanket license for digital uses, and creating the mechanical licensing collective and digital licensee coordinator [2018-115-264-115-2] [2018-115-264-115-4] [2018-115-264-115-6] [2018-115-264-115-7]. It also rewrote section 301(c) to place pre-1972 sound recordings outside title 17 copyright protection, and added section 1401 to set unauthorized use rules and transition periods for those recordings [2018-115-264-301-1] [2018-115-264-1401-1].",
   "summary_key": "dad8a3472d9c41b849eb5fc2c73a439f858570537f97e324bcb146e8bfa44ec9",
   "summary_source": "model, checked"
  },
